 Garage washing tool pictures (2026-10-24, GSP01): game/assets/menu/garage/hose-v1.png and mitt-v1.png are original built-in OpenAI image_gen outputs, copied byte-exactly with their transparency preserved. The hose nozzle and chenille wash mitt contain no requested logo or external source art. Exact prompts/provider paths/import treatment: game/assets/menu/garage/provenance-v1.json; generated bytes and SHA-256: docs/evidence/garage-studio-polish-2026-10-24/report.json. Godot bounds each imported image to512 pixels with mipmaps. No runtime AI call, third-party artwork or new dependency. This records AI-generation provenance, not independent photography or third-party licence clearance. Native review and owner/device acceptance: docs/GARAGE_STUDIO_POLISH_2026_10_24.md.
 
 Refined challenge illustrations (2026-10-23, CIR01-CIR03): game/assets/menu/challenges/entry-find-play-v2.png, entry-create-v2.png, one-to-one-v2.png, group-race-v2.png and three-by-three-v2.png are original built-in image_gen edits of the five previously generated project illustrations. The owner rejects the intervening native diagrams and requests the earlier scenic direction with less excessive surface detail and more accurate objects. The forest/garage/two-car/six-car/three-circuit subjects remain distinct. A targeted garage-car cleanup removes the original manufacturer-like badge and tiny lettering. Exact prompts, local reference paths, output paths and SHA-256: game/assets/menu/challenges/refinement-v2.json. Provider PNGs are copied byte-exactly into the workspace, with lossless mipmapped1024px-long-side Godot imports. Original v1 bytes/provenance remain. No new runtime provider, external artwork, trademark or dependency is added; fictional vehicles are decorative art and do not substitute actual in-game car selection. Actual native previews and acceptance limits: docs/evidence/challenge-art-refinement-2026-10-23/report.json.
